# Exclude non-deployable files from the packaged chart so the Helm
# release-history Secret (sh.helm.release.v1.gardenio.vN) stays under the
# K8s 1 MiB Secret limit. gardenio/scripts/release-deploy.sh runs `helm upgrade
# --install` directly from this dir (with deploy-values/gardenio-k3s.yaml), so every
# file here is gzipped into every release Secret. See ka-0000005786.
#
# dashboards/ is ignored (ka-0000002799 / ka-0000003724): the Grafana dashboard
# JSON is NO LONGER rendered into chart ConfigMaps via .Files.Get — it rides in
# the grafana-bridge image and is provisioned at runtime as type=dashboard beads.
# Keeping it in the packaged chart would re-introduce the ~296KB chart.files copy
# (half of the ~200KB-gzipped double-store that overflowed the 1 MiB Secret and
# stranded prod). The JSON stays in git as the source of truth; it is consumed by
# being copied into the bridge image at build time, not by the chart.
#
# DO NOT add files/ — it is consumed at render time via .Files.Get
# (litellm/callback-configmap.yaml). Ignoring it breaks litellm.
#
# The Keycloak login theme is NOT under files/ any more (gd-qiUiXvTX0k): it
# lives in gardenio/keycloak-theme and the release deployer ships it as a
# ConfigMap the chart only references. Do not move it back: every byte under
# files/ is stored in the release Secret, and the theme was stored twice.
#
# values-fleet.yaml / values-test.yaml are overlays for `helm -f` and the
# chart tests; they read them from the source tree, never from the package.
# Ignored because every root-level file a package carries is stored in the
# release Secret as chart.files (scripts/check-helm-release-size.sh).
.git
.gitignore
*.md
tests/
*_test.go
values-inbox.yaml
values-fleet.yaml
values-test.yaml
dashboards/
